LC 49 — Group Anagrams
Pattern:Hashing

Logic:
Anagrams have the same sorted characters.
Sort each word.
Use sorted word as the key.
Words with same key go into the same group.

Algorithm:
Sort each word
Use sorted word as key
Put word into that group
Return all groups

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    vector<vector<string>> groupAnagrams(vector<string>& strs) {
        unordered_map<string, vector<string>> mp;

        for (string s : strs) {
            string key = s;
            sort(key.begin(), key.end());
            mp[key].push_back(s);
        }

        vector<vector<string>> ans;

        for (auto& [key, group] : mp)
            ans.push_back(group);

        return ans;
    }
};

strs = ["eat","tea","tan","ate","nat","bat"]

"eat" → "aet"
"tea" → "aet"
"tan" → "ant"
"ate" → "aet"
"nat" → "ant"
"bat" → "abt"

Groups:
["eat","tea","ate"]
["tan","nat"]
["bat"]

Answer = these groups ✅

Complexity:

Time: O(n × k log k)
Space: O(n × k)

